      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/corydoras-similis",
      "html": "<p>This is a very cool uncommon species of corydoras. It is sometimes known as the violet cory catfish. They are very peaceful and suitable for many community tanks. Just don't keep them with big fish that can try to eat them, as it will likely result in the death of both fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/corydoras-similis",
      "html": "<p>Currently kept in a pH of 6-7 but they can adapt to a variety of pH.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/corydoras-similis",
      "html": "<p>Currently feeding on blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/corydoras-similis",
      "html": "<p>They are best kept in groups as they like to school here and there.</p>"
    }
  ],
